 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 666395,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Given <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">a = 9</code> and <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">b = 10</code>, does the test pass?\n<pre class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">if (a%2 == 0 and b%2 == 1) or (a%2 == 1 and b%2 == 0):\n&nbsp;&nbsp;# Test passed\nelse:\n&nbsp;&nbsp;# Test failed\n</pre>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1328243,
     "content_html": "yes",
     "correctness": "1.0",
     "feedback_html": "<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">(9%2==0 and 10%2 ==1)</code> evaluates to <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">(False and False)</code>, which is <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">False</code>. <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">(9%2 == 1 and 10%2 == 0)</code> evaluates to <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">(True and True)</code>, which is <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">True</code>. <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">False or True</code> is <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">True</code>. The <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">if</code> statement checks whether the numbers form an even-odd or odd-even pair."
    },
    {
     "id": 1328244,
     "content_html": "no",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "(9%2==0 and 10%2 ==1) evaluates to (False and False), which is (False). (9%2 == 1 and 10%2 == 0) evaluates to (True and True), which is (True). (False) or (True) is True. The if statement checks if the numbers form an even-odd or odd-even pair."
    }
   ],
